          "An asset is impaired if its Recoverable Amount is less than the Carrying Amount Carrying amount of an asset is the amount at which an asset is recognized in the balance sheet after deducting accumulated depreciation and accumulated impairment losses Recoverable amount is taken as the HIGHER of: Fair Value less costs of disposal; and Value in Use"
