          "IAS 36 requires that at each reporting date, an entity must assess whether there are indications of impairment. If there are indicators of impairment, then an impairment review/ test is conducted If there are no indicators of impairment, no further action is taken Indicators of impairment may be from External environment (external sources) Within the entity itself (internal sources)"
